# Scaffolding created by external launcher tooling. The Gradle dev flow uses run/ via
# runServer; see CLAUDE.md "How runServer actually works".
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, git matches the pattern at every
# depth, and because macOS sets core.ignorecase=true it also matched `Server/` -- which is the
# mandatory name of an asset pack's server-side asset directory
# (`AssetRegistryLoader.java:237` resolves `<packRoot>/Server`). That silently swallowed
# fpv-plugin/src/main/resources/Server/Models/, so the drone's model asset built into the jar
# but never made it into git.
/server/
*.bak
# Agent worktrees (parallel-work skill)
.worktrees/

# Agent worktrees (Claude Code isolation)
.claude/worktrees/
